{"step":6,"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731","prompt":"","response":"The task is complete. I applied the corrected formula to cells C2:C100 in Sheet1:\n\n`=IF(OR(A2=\"\",B2=\"\"),\"\",MOD(B2-TIME(0,30,0),1))`\n\nThis addresses both issues:\n1. **Midnight crossing**: Wrapping the subtraction in `MOD(...,1)` keeps the result as a time-of-day value, so a STD of 00:15 correctly becomes 23:45 (the previous day's time) instead of showing a full date like `1899-12-29 23:45`.\n2. **Blank handling**: The `IF(OR(A2=\"\",B2=\"\"),\"\",...)` guard makes column C show a blank cell when either the DATE or STD column is empty, rather than producing an error/date value.\n\nThe recalculation confirmed all values are correct and no error cells remain (rows 54+ are blank since their source data is empty).","input_tokens":9295,"output_tokens":202,"latency_ms":1746,"error":null}
